{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ונדריך", :translit "u-nedarekha", :gloss "and your vows"} {:he "ונדריך תשא ובאת", :translit "u-nedarekha tisa ve-vata", :gloss "you shall carry and come with your vows"} {:he "ונדריך תשלם", :translit "u-nedarekha teshalem", :gloss "you shall complete your vows"} {:he "אם מתו או נגנבו חייב באחריותן", :translit "im metu o nigenu khayav be-akhiyutan", :gloss "if they died or were stolen he is liable for their guarantee"} {:he "עלי", :translit "ali", :gloss "upon me"} {:he "כמאן דטעין ליה אכתפיה דמי", :translit "ke-man de-ta'in lei akhatefei damei", :gloss "it is like one who loaded them onto his shoulder"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ונדריך תשא ובאת" "ונדריך תשלם"]}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah in Nedarim (Mishnah Nedarim 3:2, treated by the passage at Nedarim 35b) teaches that one who says a formula of 'upon me' (עלי) for a sacrifice bears responsibility if the animal dies or is stolen, as the phrasing 'עלי' is interpreted to mean he has taken it upon himself like a load on his shoulder. Ba'al HaTurim links the verb תשא ('you shall carry') in Deuteronomy 12:26 to that legal exposure: the moment the vow is articulated, the person is liable for the offering's safekeeping until it is physically brought.", :sources ["Mishnah Nedarim 3:2" "Nedarim 35b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ונדריך תשא ובאת" "ונדריך תשלם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ונדריך תשא ובאת", :refs ["Deuteronomy 12:26"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ונדריך תשלם", :refs ["Job 22:27"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:21.774167570Z", :model "glm-5.2"}